#  Remote File Inclusion (RFI) and Local File Inclusion (LFI)
Remote File Inclusion (RFI) and Local File Inclusion (LFI) are vulnerabilities that allow an attacker to include files from a remote server or the local file system in a web application. This can lead to the execution of malicious code or unauthorized access to sensitive information.


